From: Harry Kim <309633041+hwisoo-kim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 18:38:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Page early when review rounds stop converging

MAX_REVIEW_ROUNDS is the only exit from the fix loop today. On PR #521 it
burned all five rounds re-litigating overlapping findings before anyone was
paged. detectStalledRounds pages at round 3 instead, naming the findings
being recycled.

The obvious design is wrong and the reasoning is the point.
review-panel.mjs DELIBERATELY re-merges unresolved priors into every round
(the cross-round re-check that guards against false negatives), so a
healthy PR that fixed 2 of 5 findings still shows 3 identical findings next
round. Keying on overlap alone would page on essentially every PR. What
separates #521 is that the blocking count did not FALL, so a pair stalls
only when it is both highly overlapping and not shrinking, and two
consecutive such pairs are required.

Both tunables were guessed in the design and both were wrong. Measured
against PR #564's four verbatim design-fit rephrasings of one defect,
versus four unrelated real findings from #564/#548:

  metric    same defect    different defect
  jaccard   0.19 - 0.52    0.00 - 0.04
  dice      0.32 - 0.68    0.00 - 0.09
  overlap   0.39 - 0.71    0.00 - 0.08

Jaccard at the planned 0.6 would have matched NONE of the four real
rephrasings -- the feature would have been dead code. Ships the overlap
(containment) coefficient at 0.3: widest margin, and the right semantics
since the panel restates one defect at different levels of detail and
Jaccard penalises the longer wording for carrying more specifics. Backed
by an absolute 3-shared-token floor (true pairs share 7-17, false pairs at
most 1). Matching is many-to-one for the same reason: greedy one-to-one
scored #564's "2 priors became 4 rephrasings" at 0.5 and missed.

Fails toward NOT paging -- malformed, unreadable, or infra/quota rounds
break the run rather than manufacture a page. MAX_REVIEW_ROUNDS still
backstops, and summoning a human off a converging loop is the costlier
error. Fuzzy matching stays out of dedupeFindings, which DROPS findings.

No new API calls in the happy path: the guard already paginates commits and
their check runs. output.text can be absent from the list response, so it
is back-filled for the newest STALL_REPEATS+1 commits only, where missing.
Tuned by env, not a 6th positional arg, so it ships without a workflow edit.

